state of decay - wants you to live out  your zombie survivalist fantasy the game  builds on the idea of the original game  but adds new features and improvements  so as we get closer to the game's  release here's a couple of the new  things you can expect in state of decay  - one of state of decay twos most  welcome additions is co-op unlike the  first one you can now live out your  zombie survivalist fantasies with up to  three players you can either join a game  or invite friends into your world I need  help  however guests do have limited  functionality they cannot pickup  missions enlist help or collect  resources for their reserves this means  that all the resources you collect will  go to the hosts  fortunately you will get to keep your  own rewards for helping other players  and whatever loot you collect is yours  to keep vehicles are a key tool in state  of decay - not only are they a great way  to get around fast but the trunk space  allows you to store multiple ransacks  saving you on more than one trip a nice  quality of life changed this time around  is when you park your vehicle in one of  your parking lots you can go to the  trunk and press right trigger to send  your supplies to your house saving you  time running back and forth the biggest  change to vehicles though is fuel  despite there being a description for  fuel resource this was never something  you really needed to worry about in the  first state of decay now every vehicle  needs to be fueled up if you want to go  so it's smart to always keep a gas  canister in the trunk so you don't get  stuck far away from home without any gas  state of decay to allows you to pick a  leader for your ragtag community once  one of your characters becomes a hero  you'll have the option to promote him or  her to a leader this doesn't change a  whole lot but it will unlock a new set  of side missions that have to do with  keeping the peace and getting to build  relationships with other communities  also be careful about who you pick as a  leader mattingly over here brought down  morale because he was bragging about  being a leader grow up Mattingly during  your travels you may come across some  modifications by outfitting different  facilities with these you can improve  productivity or alter the effects of  different sites keep in mind you can  only have one mod installed at a time  and since it takes time to install new  ones  choose your mods wisely it's also worth  noting that when you start your base has  no power this will limit most of your  facilities fortunately if you have a  generator you can power one facility for  a little bit of fuel state of decay to  s3 is the Blood Plague you'll notice  some zombies have glowing red eyes  these are plague zombies and you'll want  to be careful I better keep an eye out  for plague zombies direct contact fills  up this meter and getting it all the way  up gives your survivors the blood plague  those with the blood plague are slow and  useless if not cured they will become a  plague zombie risking further infection  to your community a cure can be made by  finding samples from plague zombies so  take care if you can't make a cure in  time it might be best to exile that  infected person before it's too late  you'll also need to deal with plague  hearts which are these horrible piles of  flesh that create plague zombies similar  to an infestation you'll need to take  these out before they spread out of  control while melee is possible it's not  ideal and you'll want to use explosives  fire and gunshots to destroy them there  are multiple plague hearts scattered  around the map and with each one you  destroy the others become stronger so  prepare yourself whenever you try and  take one out  hopefully this video gives you an idea  of what to expect from state of decay to  let us know what you're most excited  about when you get your hands on the  game and have a wonderful day the creeps  are swarming our home right now
 

